rough electronic and mobile delivery channels. First Merchants Corporation was founded in 1893 and is headquartered in Muncie, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark K. Hardwick CPA | CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $318K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["First Merchants Corporation is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.6B market cap on $663M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","36 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How (FRME) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/78/How_FRME_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_111126091802_1794406682.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794406682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"First Merchants (NASDAQ:FRME) and Pinnacle Financial Partners (NYSE:PNFP) Financial Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/first-merchants-nasdaqfrme-and-pinnacle-financial-partners-nysepnfp-financial-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793809736.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"First Merchants (FRME), Why Is It Getting Fresh Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-frme/first-merchants/news/first-merchants-frme-why-is-it-getting-fresh-attention-now","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793774428.221,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.965,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(FRME) Pr